=== day
n: 11
title: Make it yours and publish
subtitle: Personalise, download, put online, demo
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: site | js | site.js
slot: theme | css | my-theme.css
slot: extra | js | extra.js
slot: url | html | my-url.txt
slot: demo | html | demo.txt
file: site.js = site
file: my-theme.css = theme
file: extra.js = extra
refs: @page, app.js, helpers.js, style.css

--- intro
The last day. This morning's lecture went back over the whole course. This afternoon, ShowShelf becomes **your** website: your name, your colours, a feature or two of your own, and an address on the internet that you can send to anyone.

The app is the one you finished on Day 9. Its files are read-only today (open the tabs above the code box to read them). You write in three new files instead:

- **site.js**: your site's name, a sentence about it, and your name (steps 1 and 2)
- **my-theme.css**: your colours, corners and font (steps 3 and 4)
- **extra.js**: new features that use the app's own functions (steps 5 to 7)

Then you download your website as one file, put it online (steps 8 and 9), and prepare a **2-minute demo** for the end of the day (step 10). Aim to finish step 9 with at least 30 minutes to spare.

**What next?** Keep practising a little every week. [freeCodeCamp](https://www.freecodecamp.org) has free, step-by-step courses, and [MDN Web Docs](https://developer.mozilla.org) explains every HTML element, CSS property and JavaScript method. A great next project: build ShowShelf again from scratch with a different free API, for example one for music or for books.

--- template
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="A TV show finder with a watchlist, built with HTML, CSS and JavaScript.">
  <title>ShowShelf</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="my-theme.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="container header-inner">
      <a href="index.html" class="logo" id="logo">ShowShelf</a>
      <nav class="nav">
        <a href="index.html" id="nav-home">Home</a>
        <a href="index.html" id="nav-mylist">My List <span class="list-count" id="list-count">0</span></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="container">
    <!-- View 1: home, with the search and the grid of shows -->
    <section id="home-view">
      <div class="hero">
        <h1>What are we watching tonight?</h1>
        <p id="tagline">Search real shows from TVmaze and keep your watchlist.</p>
        <form class="search" id="search-form">
          <input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Search shows, e.g. office" aria-label="Search shows">
          <button type="submit">Search</button>
        </form>
      </div>
      <div class="toolbar">
        <div class="genres" id="genres"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="status" id="status" hidden></p>
      <p class="status" id="empty-message" hidden>No shows match your search.</p>
      <div class="grid" id="grid"></div>
    </section>

    <!-- View 2: one show -->
    <section id="show-view" hidden>
      <p class="back-link"><button type="button" class="button-secondary" id="back-button">← Back to shows</button></p>
      <p class="status" id="show-status" hidden></p>
      <article class="show" id="show-details">
        <div class="show-header">
          <img class="poster" id="show-poster" src="poster.svg" alt="">
          <div>
            <h1 id="show-name"></h1>
            <p class="meta" id="show-meta"></p>
            <p class="rating" id="show-rating"></p>
            <p id="show-genres"></p>
            <p class="intro" id="show-summary"></p>
            <p class="show-links"><button type="button" id="show-list-button">+ Add to My List</button></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <section>
          <h2>Cast</h2>
          <ul id="show-cast"></ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Seasons</h2>
          <table class="seasons">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Season</th><th>Episodes</th><th>Year</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="show-seasons"></tbody>
          </table>
        </section>
      </article>
    </section>

    <!-- View 3: My List -->
    <section id="mylist-view" hidden>
      <div class="hero">
        <h1>My List</h1>
        <p>The shows you saved. They stay here after a reload.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="status" id="mylist-empty">Your list is empty. Press + on a show to add it.</p>
      <div class="grid" id="mylist-grid"></div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <!-- "Made by ..." is filled in from site.js -->
    <p id="made-by" hidden></p>
    <!-- TVmaze's data is free to use if we say where it comes from -->
    <p>Built in the Web Dev in 11 Days course · <a href="https://www.tvmaze.com">Data from TVmaze</a></p>
  </footer>

  <!-- The order matters: each file can use what the files above it made -->
  <script src="helpers.js"></script>
  <script src="site.js"></script>
  <script src="app.js"></script>
  <script src="extra.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

